    "No query-specific Caco-2/PAMPA permeability or intestinal absorption data.",
    "No active-uptake transporter evidence for pyridostigmine; neostigmine P-gp data are analog-only.",
    "No fasted-state dissolution or formulation data for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: pyridostigmine is a permanently charged quaternary pyridinium dimethylcarbamate; transferable carbamate contexts (physostigmine poor F; bambuterol ~10%) and L5 neostigmine intestinal-loop absorption (12.8% after 2 h, 5.5% with secretion, 6.6% gut-wall trapping) support F < 20%. L5 efflux/pH/osmotic and unrelated paraquat/MPP+/ESC8 records do not overturn this; confidence remains moderate due to lack of direct query F."
}

